Reference frames, rotating motion and consistent forces (@fd-frames: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @fluid-dynamics, #source "../sources/Analytical-Fluid-Mechanics-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_075CGXNA8WHV26ZW53C7XTQ48V", #source "../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Dynamics-Mei-MIT.lingua#r_21NXVH78F0NYDPDVTG66PG261P", #source "../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-Tong.lingua#r_3SP698XHQFSZZ6N9Q22NESHMEA", #fluid-dynamics "../../thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer/entropy/Local-entropy-production-and-transport-assumptions.lingua#r_0XE4QFR9SE1KBW2RDHYPVVJZZE") { r_5SB0X4AF38MZ5W9V6TX733B6BN
**Read:** [Fluid Mechanics — Richard Fitzpatrick](../sources/Analytical-Fluid-Mechanics-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_075CGXNA8WHV26ZW53C7XTQ48V), rotating-fluid and coordinate treatments; [Advanced fluid dynamics — Mei notes and MIT modules](../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Dynamics-Mei-MIT.lingua#r_21NXVH78F0NYDPDVTG66PG261P), rotating-fluid modules; [Fluid Mechanics — David Tong](../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-Tong.lingua#r_3SP698XHQFSZZ6N9Q22NESHMEA), rotating shallow-water development after the basic equations.

An inertial-frame equation and a rotating-frame equation can describe the same motion. Transform velocity and acceleration consistently. A uniformly rotating frame introduces Coriolis and centrifugal terms; a changing rotation rate also introduces an Euler acceleration term. The frame choice is not an additional measured force acting in isolation.

Uniform translation does not change the physical deformation rate of a fluid element. Rigid-body rotation changes component descriptions while the material law must retain its physical meaning. This requirement becomes especially important for constitutive models with memory.

Write the same simple rotating-container balance in both frames and recover the same pressure field. Identify the difference between a rotating coordinate system and an actual solid boundary that transfers angular momentum during spin-up. Reserve planetary or rotor-specific simplifications for the scale analysis that justifies them.

